<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="How The Physics Lab handles your privacy: no accounts, Google Analytics usage statistics, no ads, and practice scores kept in your browser." schemaType="Article"><article class="article"><Breadcrumbs items={[['Home','/'],['Privacy policy']]}/><div class="eyebrow">Plain-language privacy</div><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="lesson-lead">The Physics Lab is free to use and never asks you to sign up. This page explains what is collected when you visit, who collects it, and how to opt out.</p><p class="small-note">Last updated: 12 November 2026</p><h2>No accounts, no forms</h2><p>There are no accounts, logins, or sign-up forms. The Physics Lab does not ask for your name, email address, or other personal details. Simulations, calculations, and worksheets run in your browser. The teacher activities and answer keys work the same way: students complete them on paper or in their teacher’s own assignment, so no student work or names ever reach this site.</p><h2>Usage statistics (Google Analytics)</h2><p>We use Google Analytics (measurement ID G-2ZHXFW2460) to count visits and see which pages are useful. Google Analytics uses cookies to record things like the pages you view, how you arrived, your approximate location, and your device and browser type. We use these reports only in aggregate, to improve the lab. Google processes this data under the <a class="text-link" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>; see also <a class="text-link" href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>No advertising</h2><p>The Physics Lab shows no ads. No advertising code is loaded on any page, and no advertising cookies are set.</p><h2>Stored on your device</h2><p>Practice saves only your best score for each topic in your browser’s local storage, so it stays on this device and is never sent to us. Local storage also keeps your cookie choice (<code>cookieConsent</code>, see below); it holds nothing else. Shared experiment links contain the input values and time you chose, so anyone with the link can reproduce that setup.</p><h2>Fonts and hosting</h2><p>Google Fonts supplies the typefaces and receives the usual font requests from your browser. Our hosting provider may keep standard access logs, such as IP addresses and requested pages, to deliver and protect the site.</p><h2>Cookie choices</h2><p>Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland see a small cookie banner. Until you choose, Google Analytics runs without cookies. <strong>Accept</strong> allows analytics cookies; <strong>Reject</strong> keeps analytics cookie-free. Your choice is stored in your browser for 180 days (as <code>cookieConsent</code>), and you can change it at any time with <em>Cookie settings</em> in the footer.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><ul><li>Block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or browse in a private window.</li><li>Use a tracker blocker. The lab works without analytics.</li><li>Install the <a class="text-link" href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a> to stop Google Analytics on every site.</li><li>Clear this site’s data in your browser to remove saved practice scores.</li></ul><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>If how the site handles data changes, we will update this page and the date above. To learn more about how the lab’s models and data work, read <a class="text-link" href="/about/">About The Physics Lab</a>.</p></article></Layout>
